Terraform Import — Importing Real Infrastructure into Terraform State

Terraform import is a simple but powerful command. It helps Terraform take control of resources that already exist in your cloud.

Many teams use it when resources were created manually or during a migration to IaC. Instead of deleting and recreating, you just import them into the state.

You define the resource block in your .tf file.
Then run:

terraform import <resource_address> <resource_id>

This only updates the state file.
It does not generate code or auto-fill configuration.

After importing, always run a terraform plan.

It shows whether your .tf file actually matches the real infrastructure.

Import is not about creating resources.
It’s about giving Terraform ownership of what already exists.
